I sit at Marine Drive for a long time.
The breeze is very nice.
Now it is time to go home.
I stand up.
I look towards the road.
Where is the return bus stop?
This time I do not ask anyone.
I remember the route.
I walk straight towards the main road.
I turn left at the corner.
The bus stop is in front of me.
My bus comes soon.
I board the bus.
I sit near the window.
I look outside.
Now I know the routes.
This city is not new now.
I am very proud of myself.
